This project is a new implementation informed by public research and permissively
licensed open-source work. Before copying source code from any upstream project,
preserve all notices required by that project's license.

Reference implementations currently being evaluated:
- Hla-aung/liquid-glass (MIT): WebGL2/Three.js shared renderer, DOM capture,
  Snell's-law-inspired optical model, lens profiles, Fresnel/specular treatment.
- el-gladiador/liquid-glass-react (MIT): shared WebGL2 context, multi-layer
  refraction, Gaussian blur, capture invalidation/cooldown, off-screen pausing.
- archisvaze/liquid-glass: useful visual/WebGL reference; do not copy source until
  its license is independently verified.
